     FormBox["\"readout: the accumulated record Q(t)\"", TraditionalForm], 
     PlotRange -> {{0, 3.}, {-0.49504796097191134`, 1.6033746939765043`}}, 
     PlotRangeClipping -> True, PlotRangePadding -> {{
        Scaled[0.02], 
        Scaled[0.02]}, {
        Scaled[0.02], 
        Scaled[0.02]}}, Ticks -> {Automatic, Automatic}}]},
  "RowDefault"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[17]= ",ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the state path fluctuates around the Lindblad mean, as a \
single record must, while the readout ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 " climbs steeply where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " is near one and bends as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 " falls, its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"C", "I"}], "TI"]]], " ", 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " signal buried under noise. The two panels share one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 ", and that is the physical content of a measurement record: the noise \
written into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 " is the same noise that kicked ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell["The ensemble: matching the mean and the spread", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A single path tells us little; the mean lives in the ensemble and the noise \
in how widely the paths spread. Rather than compare final values, we keep the \
whole trajectory from each route, average many of them, and watch the two \
ensemble means track the exact Lindblad curve across the entire interval. The \
two routes are the built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["StratonovichProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " integrator, which discretizes the target Stratonovich SDE, and the \
regularized ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 " route, whose smooth ODE approaches that same SDE as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["gen",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 "; the yardstick is a single Lindblad solution from ",
 Cell[BoxData["DSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before any simulation, the central claim can be settled exactly, by the \
same built-in we are keeping. We never hand-compute the \
It\[OHat]-Stratonovich correction, but the conversion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", 
   RowBox[{"StratonovichProcess", "[", "...", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " applies it for us, rewriting our Stratonovich vector field in It\[OHat] \
form. If the explicit Stratonovich drift truly carries the correction, its It\
\[OHat] form must be the affine drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " we encoded as ",
 Cell[BoxData["driftIto"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 " for the Lindblad reference, with the readout row untouched. Convert the \
full four-component field and subtract that target, under the physical \
assumption that the rates are nonnegative (needed only to fold ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"C", "I"}], "TI"]]], " ", 
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"B", "A"}], "TI"]]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 " into a single root):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Assuming", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", ",", " ", "\"\<CI\>\""}], "]"}], " ", ">=", 
      " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", ",", " ", "\"\<BA\>\""}], "]"}], " ", ">=", 
      " ", "0"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ItoProcess", "[", 
         RowBox[{"StratonovichProcess", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"driftStrat", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "q"}], 
                "}"}], ",", " ", "ratesSym"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{"List", " ", "/@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"diffStrat", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "q"}], 
                 "}"}], ",", " ", "ratesSym"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "q"}], 
              "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "q"}], 
              "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "q0"}], 
              "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
        "[", "\"\<Drift\>\"", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "x"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "y"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"z", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "z"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"q", "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "q"}]}], "}"}]}], 
      ")"}], "\n", "   ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"driftIto", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         "ratesSym"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\[CapitalGamma]", ",", " ", "\"\<CI\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], " ",
         "z"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[18]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[18]= ",ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The difference vanishes row by row: the It\[OHat] form of the Stratonovich \
SDE we hand ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 " is exactly the affine drift on all three Bloch rows, and the readout row \
is unchanged, so the correction is carried in full and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " is the same in both calculi. This settles the central claim at no \
numerical cost and more decisively than any Monte-Carlo match; the ensemble \
below only confirms what the algebra already proves. One corollary in one \
line: switch the measurement off and the two calculi must coincide, because \
only the measurement noise separates them:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"driftStrat", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "q"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "ratesSym"}], "]"}], " ", "-", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"driftIto", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         "ratesSym"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"ratesSym", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "z"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}],
    " ", "/.", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ratesSym", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ratesSym", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[19]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->
  "Out[19]= ",ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"C", "I"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"B", "A"}], "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 " the entire gap between the Stratonovich and It\[OHat] drifts closes: the \
correction is measurement backaction and nothing else."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell["Start the worker kernels:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"LaunchKernels", "[", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[20]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Share the definitions the regularized trajectory needs, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["ParallelTable"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 " can spread the paths across cores:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"DistributeDefinitions", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "driftStrat", ",", " ", "diffStrat", ",", " ", "wienerFun", ",", " ", 
    "oneTraj"}], "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[21]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Generate ",
 Cell[BoxData["ntraj"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 " full trajectories from the built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["StratonovichProcess"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " integrator, keeping every step of each path. Feed it the same Stratonovich \
drift and diffusion the ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 " route uses, all four rows, and ask for the order-3/2 scalar-noise method \
rather than the default Euler-Maruyama, whose average carries a bias \
proportional to the step and so drifts off the exact curve at any finite \
step. The process variables are Wolfram's formal symbols, unbound by \
construction, so they are safe placeholders:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "stratRun", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stratRun", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "r_", ",", " ", "init_", ",", " ", "tf_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", 
     "ntraj_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "v", ",", " ", "proc", ",", " ", "td"}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[FormalX]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[FormalY]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[FormalZ]", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[FormalQ]", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"proc", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"StratonovichProcess", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"driftStrat", "[", 
            RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"List", " ", "/@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"diffStrat", "[", 
             RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "v"}], "}"}], ",",
          "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "\[FormalX]", ",", " ", "\[FormalY]", ",", " ", "\[FormalZ]", ",",
              " ", "\[FormalQ]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "init"}], "}"}], ",", " ",
          "t"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"td", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"RandomFunction", "[", 
          RowBox[{"proc", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0.", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           "ntraj", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
           "Method", " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<StochasticRungeKuttaScalarNoise\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"td", "[", "\"\<ValueList\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[22]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Generate the same count of regularized trajectories, each ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],
 " solution read off on a shared time grid, keeping all four components so \
the record stays beside the state that produced it. Two arguments carry \
defaults so the one real relationship lives in one place: the integrator step \
is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["gen",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 ", held a factor of four below the noise grid, and the read-off grid is the \
noise grid itself:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "regRun", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"regRun", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "r_", ",", " ", "init_", ",", " ", "tf_", ",", " ", "dtGen_", ",", " ", 
     "ntraj_", ",", " ", "baseSeed_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"maxstep_", " ", ":", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"grid_", " ", ":", " ", "Automatic"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ms", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"maxstep", " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Automatic", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"dtGen", "/", "4"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"grid", " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Automatic", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"noiseGrid", "[", 
           RowBox[{"tf", ",", " ", "dtGen"}], "]"}]}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"ParallelTable", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"tr", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"oneTraj", "[", 
            RowBox[{
            "r", ",", " ", "init", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dtGen", ",", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{"baseSeed", " ", "+", " ", "i"}], ",", " ", "ms"}], 
            "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", "g", "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "tr"}], 
          "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "ntraj"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[23]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell["\<\
For the harder regimes and the step-size study below we will want only the \
final values, so reduce each generator to them. The native final Bloch \
vectors:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "stratRef", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stratRef", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "r_", ",", " ", "init_", ",", " ", "tf_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", 
     "ntraj_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"stratRun", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "r", ",", " ", "init", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "ntraj",
       ",", " ", "seed"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[24]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And the regularized final Bloch vectors, read off at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["f", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],
 " alone, the integrator step defaulting the same way:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "ensemble", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ensemble", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "r_", ",", " ", "init_", ",", " ", "tf_", ",", " ", "dtGen_", ",", " ", 
     "ntraj_", ",", " ", "baseSeed_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"maxstep_", " ", ":", " ", "Automatic"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"regRun", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "r", ",", " ", "init", ",", " ", "tf", ",", " ", "dtGen", ",", " ", 
      "ntraj", ",", " ", "baseSeed", ",", " ", "maxstep", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "tf", "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "3"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[25]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run both on the representative case, on the shared grid set by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"dtGenOf", "[", "ratesB", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 ". First the native ensemble:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stratRunB", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"stratRun", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ratesB", ",", " ", "initB", ",", " ", "tfB", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dtGenOf", "[", "ratesB", "]"}], ",", " ", "nB", ",", " ", 
     "2024"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[26]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell["Then the regularized ensemble on the same grid:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"regRunB", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"regRun", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ratesB", ",", " ", "initB", ",", " ", "tfB", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dtGenOf", "[", "ratesB", "]"}], ",", " ", "nB", ",", " ", 
     "9100"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[27]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Average each ensemble over its trajectories and compare the two mean paths \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " against the single exact Lindblad trajectory:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"noiseGrid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tfB", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dtGenOf", "[", "ratesB", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"lb", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"lindbladBloch", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ratesB", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"initB", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "stratRunB", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
        "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "regRunB", "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",",
        "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"lb", "[", "#", "]"}], "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
           "g"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
           RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Thick", ",", " ", "Black"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<StratonovichProcess mean\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<regularized mean\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<Lindblad \[LeftAngleBracket]z\[RightAngleBracket](t)\>\""}],
        "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<t\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<\[LeftAngleBracket]z\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<averaging the trajectories rebuilds the master \
equation\>\""}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->
  "In[28]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

